ext untap step.)", "You may have Vizier of Many Faces enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except if Vizier of Many Faces was embalmed, the token has no mana cost, it's white, and it's a Zombie in addition to its other types.\\nEmbalm {3}{U}{U}", 'You may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast creature spells from the top of your library.\\nYou can spend mana of any type to cast creature spells.', "Zombies you control get +1/+1.\\nWhen Liliana's Mastery enters the battlefield, create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.", 'Zombies you control get +2/+1 until end of turn. Other creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', '[+1]: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token. Mill two cards.\\n[−3]: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. That creature is a black Zombie in addition to its other colors and types.\\n[−7]: Destroy all non-Zombie creatures.', '[+1]: Until your next turn, prevent all damage target permanent would deal.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon of the Trials becomes a 4/4 Human Soldier creature with indestructible that\'s still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[0]: You get an emblem with "As long as you control a Gideon planeswalker, you can\'t lose the game and your opponents can\'t win the game."', '[+2]: Put a -1/-1 counter on up to one target creature.\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature with a -1/-1 counter on it.\\n[−10]: Return all creature cards from your graveyard to the battlefield.', "[+2]: Scry 2.\\n[0]: Look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card or a creature card with mana value less than or equal to the number of loyalty counters on Nissa, Steward of Elements, you may put that card onto the battlefield.\\n[−6]: Untap up to two target lands you control. They become 5/5 Elemental creatures with flying and haste until end of turn. They're still lands.", "[+2]: Untap all creatures you control. Those creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon, Martial Paragon becomes a 5/5 Human Soldier creature with indestructible that's still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[−10]: Creatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn. Tap all creatures your opponents control.", '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Scribe of the Mindful: Return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', "{1}, {T}: Target creature can't attack this turn. Put a brick counter on Edifice of Authority.\\n{1}, {T}: Until your next turn, target creature can't attack or block and its activated abilities can't be activated. Activate only if there are three or more brick counters on Edifice of Authority.", '{1}, {T}: You gain 1 life. Put a brick counter on Luxa River Shrine.\\n{T}: You gain 2 life. Activate only if there are three or more brick counters on Luxa River Shrine.', "{2}, Discard a card: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature. That creature can't block this turn.", '{2}, {T}: Add one mana of any color. Put a brick counter on Pyramid of the Pantheon.\\n{T}: Add three mana of any one color. Activate only if there are three or more brick counters on Pyramid of the Pantheon.', "{2}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until end of turn, you may play that card. Put a brick counter on Oracle's Vault.\\n{T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until end of turn, you may play that card without paying its mana cost. Activate only if there are three or more brick counters on Oracle's Vault.", '{2}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{2}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Oashra Cultivator: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{3}{B}: Target opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life. Activate only if you control a Liliana planeswalker.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Grasping Dunes: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Cradle of the Accursed: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', "{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card. Activate only if you've cast a noncreature spell this turn.", '{T}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn.', "{T}: Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Untap another target permanent.\\nCycling {1}{U} ({1}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Vizier of Tumbling Sands, untap target permanent.']
flavor: ['"A single grain of sand is insignificant, but a sandstorm can reduce pyramids to dust. Stand with your crop. Become the storm."\\n—Oketra, god of solidarity', '"All are not equal—neither in life nor after death. Bontu\'s favorites will stand highest in eternity."\\n—Senifet, vizier of Bontu', '"All questions will be answered during the Hour of Revelation."', '"Allow zealous flames to light your path and the glory you seek will be revealed."\\n—Hazoret, god of zeal', '"Ambition requires clarity. If you have any doubts, they must be abandoned."\\n—Bontu, god of ambition', '"Angels? My feelings remain unchanged."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"As a child I saw something walking in the distance, far beyond the Hekma—shadow-dark, and taller than the gods. Even now, it passes through my dreams."\\n—Pytamun, initiate of Nef crop', '"Ashes can\'t be embalmed."\\n—Neheb, initiate of Ahn crop', '"Combat is a form of worship, the clash of steel a solemn prayer."\\n—Pytamun, initiate of Nef crop', '"Death has seeped into every part of this plane. I can feel it on my skin and taste it like sand in my mouth."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Dissent? Your gods can\'t even begin to comprehend the dissent that\'s about to happen here!"\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Don\'t you ever wonder what lies beyond the Hekma? Beyond the reach of the gods? Beyond the horns on the horizon?"\\n—Samut, initiate of Tah crop', '"Eternal glory awaits you, my child."', '"Everything in the trial has teeth. You will overcome them, or you will feed them."\\n—Rhonas, god of strength', '"Eyes see only what is possible. A trained mind can explore the impossible."\\n—Kefnet, god of knowledge', '"Fight through it."', '"Fly as an arrow through the trials, and never waver in your course."\\n—Oketra, god of solidarity', '"Hesitation breeds dissension. To be worthy of the next life, you must never look back."\\n—Anep, vizier of Hazoret', '"How can there be doubt in the presence of such blessings?"\\n—Ukhat, vizier of initiation', '"I do things in my own time."\\n—Etha, initiate of Rhet crop', '"I feel the presence of the God-Pharaoh in the Second Sun, and I rise upon its rays."', '"I have foreseen that you will not pass my trial."', '"I\'d like to say that it\'s our pet, but the reverse may be closer to the truth."\\n—Ixor, initiate of Rhet crop', '"I\'ll fight no more just for the honor of dying. The afterlife will have to wait."', '"I\'m never unarmed."', '"If it is bigger, you must be faster. If it is stronger, you must be sharper. Anything less, and you will never seize a place in our God-Pharaoh\'s perfect afterlife."\\n—Rhonas, god of strength', '"If you do not feel the thrill of battle, alive like a flame, you will never triumph."', '"If you fear poisons, it is because you are ignorant of them."\\n—Hapatra, vizier of poisons', '"If you want to truly test your survival skills, walk the Obelisk Path when the drakes are feeding."\\n—Etha, initiate of Rhet crop', '"In the Hour of Glory, the gods and the untested will prove their worth before the God-Pharaoh."\\n—*The Accounting of Hours*', '"In the afterlife, I\'ll have no need of sleep. And until then, I have no time for it!"', '"Instincts to guide. Strength to overcome."', '"It usually appears placid, but don\'t be fooled. The Luxa River is a snake, and it can swallow you whole."\\n—Neponem, vizier of Kefnet', '"Let me try one of Kefnet\'s puzzles. This one was too easy."', '"Like fruits in the field, we will be harvested when the season is right."', '"Look! That is why we must never waver. That is what awaits us if we fail."\\n—Djeru, initiate of Tah crop', '"My mind is the calm in the midst of the storm, and my javelin the lightning."', '"My stride will break only against the twin points of Hazoret\'s spear."', '"No amount of strength can help you overcome my trial. You must be ready to forgo your body and favor your mind."\\n—Kefnet, god of knowledge', '"No one is born worthy."', '"Not all in our crop deserve the afterlife. We must leave the unworthy behind, Samut."\\n—Djeru, initiate of Tah crop', '"Occasionally, there are those who refuse to appreciate all that the God-Pharaoh provides for us."\\n—Temmet, vizier of Naktamun', '"Oketra had our crop build an obelisk to prove the power of working together. But I am stronger without the weak."', '"Prayers will curdle on the tongue and be heard by rotting ears."\\n—Minaldra, the Vizag Atum', '"Rely too much on your weapons and watch your dreams shatter in your hands."\\n—Rhonas, god of strength', '"Some hid from the storm. I embraced it and learned its name."', '"The God-Pharaoh created the Hekma to protect us from the horrors beyond and to surround us in his love."', '"The Second Sun nears its destination! Let it light the way to ours!"', '"The answers are here. This is the way through the trial."', '"The best answers solve more than one riddle."\\n—Kefnet, god of knowledge', '"The dead perform all the work here—farming, building, teaching, even embalming their fellow mummies. The living need do nothing but train. What system could be more perfect?"\\n—Temmet, vizier of Naktamun', '"The expected way through the trial is far too tedious."', '"The face of mediocrity is wrapped in anointed linen. Aspire to a better end."\\n—Epnokep, vizier of Bontu', '"The fiercest loyalties are earned in battle."\\n—Gideon Jura', '"The gods here may walk among the people, but they are not with them."\\n—Gideon Jura', '"The lands of the God-Pharaoh are suffused with his breath."', '"The more I see of this place, the less I want to."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"The nature of this plane makes it almost too easy for me to command the dead."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"The only question we need to ask is how best to fulfill the will of the God-Pharaoh."', '"The power that flows here cannot be denied. But where is the source?"\\n—Nissa Revane', '"The vizier of poisons teaches an unconventional kind of strength."', '"The worthy shall cultivate a nimble mind to perceive the glorious wonders that await them."\\n—Monument inscription', '"The worthy shall hone a strong body to endure the boundless energies of the afterlife."\\n—Monument inscription', '"The worthy shall respect the worthy. In the afterlife, all will stand united."\\n—Monument inscription', '"The worthy shall rush to the God-Pharaoh\'s side with relentless zeal, rising to overcome every obstacle."\\n—Monument inscription', '"The worthy shall strive for greatness. Supremacy in life leads to supremacy in the afterlife."\\n—Monument inscription', '"There are so many of them. It seems they\'ve just been waiting for someone to serve."', '"They are small, but they always want more. Learn from them."\\n—Bontu, god of ambition', '"They might be dead, but these mummies are masters of their trade."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"Those wings are no advantage. I will pin them to the ceiling of the Hekma."', '"Time is like the Luxa River—though it flows in one direction, it can be diverted."', '"To see gods among the people, part of their daily lives . . . It\'s inspiring."', '"To victory! To glory! To eternity!"', '"True intentions lie not in the head but in the heart."\\n—Bontu, god of ambition', '"We do not swerve."\\n—Tah-crop charioteer motto', '"We each have a weight to carry on the road to the afterlife."\\n—Oketra, god of solidarity', '"When I wish to be strong, I train. When I wish to be wise, I study. When I wish to rest, I start again."', '"When all doubts have melted away, the worthy will meet the Hour of Eternity and earn a place at the God-Pharaoh\'s side."\\n—*The Accounting of Hours*', '"When the Hour of Promise arrives, the God-Pharaoh will tear down the Hekma, for its protection will be needed no longer."\\n—*The Accounting of Hours*', '"When the Second Sun rests between the horns on the horizon, so begins the Hour of Revelation. Then the Hour of Glory, the Hour of Promise, and finally the Hour of Eternity."\\n—*The Accounting of Hours*', '"When the time comes, only one of you will be honored by my spear."\\n—Hazoret, god of zeal', '"Wherever you are in the city, you can feel the presence of the God-Pharaoh. Take comfort in that."\\n—Ukhat, vizier of initiation', '"Why cling to these trappings? They are but tools and affectations. True wealth can be possessed only in the afterlife."', '"Why so many questions?"\\n—Temmet, vizier of Naktamun', '"You are undeserving of the afterlife. You will never feel the God-Pharaoh\'s embrace."', '"You may feel a slight sting."', '"You will succeed as one or fail as many."', '"You wish to remember this lesson? I will write it down for you."\\n—Senifet, vizier of Bontu', '"You\'ll need all your strength for the trials to come."', '"Your waters sustain the living and carry the dead. Mighty Luxa, let your power flow through me!"', 'A mudflow swallowed the lowlands years ago. All that remains are a bottomless mire and an endless rain of ash.', 'A sandwurm can lie in wait beneath the sands for years until the slightest tremor alerts it to the presence of prey.', 'A true reflection of nature: death fostering life.', 'Aether currents in the sky mirror water currents below, including the deadly rapids.', "All but the gods fear the scorpion's sting.", "Amonkhet's dual suns don't allow for the darkness of night, so bats are most active under the gloom of the frequent sandstorms.", 'As Gideon watched the initiate murder his crop-mate, his admiration of the city of Naktamun gave way to horror.', 'As its parched flesh withers away, its malignant hunger grows.', 'Aspiring to earn their place in the afterlife, acolytes train every day against those who fell short of that glory.', 'Beyond the chaos of Ghirapur lies a vibrant world where aether flows through nature.', 'Blades and bravery go hand in hand.', 'Cantankerous and territorial, sandwurms claim even the skies above their dunes.', "Cartouches chronicle the initiates' achievements in the trials.", 'Centuries of scouring sands have carved and polished the rocky terrain of the Shefet.', "Debate rages among the viziers whether comparing the kudu's horns to the God-Pharaoh's is blasphemy or reverence.", "Dependence on luck is anathema to Kefnet's rigorous studies. Those who hope to escape his maze by chance never succeed.", 'Entire valleys have been formed by mummies laboring to find veins of lazotep.', 'Even gods have pets.', 'Even in the relative safety of the city, there are places best left undisturbed.', 'Few can overcome an assault of such aggressive serenity.', 'Five gods, one purpose.', 'Forever restless. Forever growing in number.', 'From the time they are hatchlings, river drakes are taught to pull the largest prey from the Luxa.', "Hazoret's gift is bestowed only once.", 'Headlong is the only way to pass through the gate to the afterlife.', 'Her subtle smile is suffused with venom.', 'Her words inspire action. Her actions inspire victory.', 'If one of the anointed fails to serve with perfect obedience, the desert is always ready to receive it.', "In Amonkhet's ever-shifting sands, nothing stays buried for long.", 'In the training ground known as the Gauntlet, initiates are pushed to practice more destructive techniques.', 'Initiates in the heat of combat must be able to adapt to changing conditions.', 'Initiates live and train with their crop, the unit that begins the trials together.', 'Initiates must train to resist the natural toxins they use as weapons.', 'Initiates need worry only about the trials. Everything else is in the hands of the gods.', 'Instinct yields the truest insight.', 'It falls to the gods to help all become worthy of the afterlife.', 'It feeds on dry bones in the sand and desperate pleas in the wind.', 'It slithers through the senses, constricting consciousness and poisoning perceptions.', "Its breath doesn't assault the senses. It pollutes the mind.", 'Khenra are almost always born as twins. Their instinctual connection lends itself well to their preferred fighting style.', 'Many initiates believe it possesses secrets known only to Kefnet himself. Many have become meals trying to learn them.', 'Many such monuments dot the wasteland known as Ifnir.', 'Minotaurs favor magic that manifests as weapons wrapped in flame.', 'Nagas wielding twin daggers excel at the fighting technique known as the Bite of Rhonas.', 'Never flinch. Never falter. Never fear.', "Oketra's closest viziers are known as her chosen, though others may have a better claim to that moniker.", 'On Amonkhet, death is an ever-present part of life.', "Only from the sky can one fully understand the horrors of the wastes and the wonder of the Hekma's protection.", "Part of the acolytes' training is to walk along the Hekma, staring out at the ravenous horrors kept at bay by the God-Pharaoh's barrier.", 'Rest sometimes requires the right prompting.', "Rhonas's monument is home to a wider variety of creatures than anywhere else in the city of Naktamun—a feature most initiates fail to appreciate.", 'She can coil a breeze like a string around her finger—or twist it into a noose.', 'Shoulder to shoulder until blade must turn against blade.', "Some naga initiates move as silently the suns' reflections on the water.", 'Strong wings make strong winds.', 'Surviving an encounter with it is proof enough that an initiate is ready for the Trial of Strength.', "Tazeem's embrace is harsh, but for those that call it home, nothing else will do.", 'The Broken Lands are littered with the remnants of civilizations long dead and infested by terrors very much alive.', 'The Curse of Wandering leaves only hatred.', 'The Hekma may repel storms and monsters, but nothing holds back the heat of the suns.', 'The Trial of Knowledge challenges and broadens the minds of initiates.', 'The anointed work the mines without pause, their cartouches instilling them with tireless purpose.', 'The arrows fell like fiery rain, and for a moment, the sky itself seemed to burn.', 'The banks of the Luxa River attract all manner of predator but only the most resilient of prey.', 'The dead who wander beyond the safety of the city crave only to spread their curse.', 'The endless expanse of desert surrounding Naktamun sometimes yields threats that the gods themselves must answer.', 'The fifth cartouche is the final affirmation of glory, granted only to the worthy dead.', 'The forked tongue of the naga is sensitive to drifting scent trails from the past, present, and sometimes even the future.', "The one thing the Gatewatch didn't expect to find on a plane ruled by Nicol Bolas was perfection.", 'The only relief in sight is a mirage.', 'The only way to finish the Trial of Strength is with a basilisk scale in hand.', 'The pain of death is nothing compared to the pain of failure.', 'The river split into many channels as it flowed to the Halimar Sea. Few travelers could follow the same one twice.', 'The scouring sands of Shefet polish its carapace, and the ranks of the cursed fill its belly.', 'The sound of its plated tail beating on desert rocks is often mistaken for the footfalls of a much larger predator.', 'The viziers serving Rhonas, the god of strength, maintain the menagerie of animals employed during his trial.', 'There are no safe paths through the Trial of Strength.', "There is only one fate left to those banished from the God-Pharaoh's city.", 'They are drawn by the brilliant blue glint of the mineral lazotep from the mines below.', 'They are tasked with protecting the entrance to the embalming chambers.', 'They are the first to greet dissenters on their journey into exile.', 'They labor beside the anointed, constructing the vast monuments of Naktamun.', 'Those who earn a glorious death are given the highest honor. They are carried on funeral barges through the gate to the afterlife.', "Though the Luxa River brings life to Naktamun, it's not without dangers.", 'Though they are held in high regard as symbols of the god Oketra, cats often lack her sense of solidarity.', 'To Hazoret, those who fight for her are her beloved children.', 'To a trained warrior, there is scarcely a more potent weapon than patience.', "To consult a sphinx is a test in patience. Perhaps that's the point.", 'To prepare for the Trial of Strength, nagas shed their old skin—and with it their scars, their doubts, and their fears.', 'Understanding is a matter of perspective.', 'Waterways carve their routes through the land to reflect the paths the aether streams cut through the clouds.', 'What the gods decree, the mummies enforce.', "What the initiates face in the final trial is completely at Hazoret's discretion.", 'With carrion a rarity in the Broken Lands, the hyenas that stalk the deserts hunt in packs.', 'With the fate of Innistrad uncertain, some seek solace in remote areas.', 'Without the God-Pharaoh, there would be no Luxa. Without the Luxa, there would be no life.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adrian Majkrzak', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Allen Williams', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Burdett', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'David Gaillet', 'David Palumbo', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'E. M. Gist', 'Efflam Mercier', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Kang', 'Jason Rainville', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lindsey Look', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Burns', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Richard Wright', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Shreya Shetty', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steven Belledin', 'Sung Choi', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Tommy Arnold', 'Tony Foti', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wesley Burt', 'Winona Nelson', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros']
